gate: OPEN
v:4 role:dev x:frontend
task: S89 T1 — Editable speeding and stop thresholds
requires: [FRONTEND_DEV]
sprint: S89

context: |
  EventsTab prints EVENTS_CONFIG.value (130 / 90) and the row is only a
  toggle. mergeVehicleConfigFromEventChecks writes those constants into
  speedingValue and minStopTime, ignoring the server value and any edit.
  Old Android exposed an input: speeding 0–360 km/h, stop in seconds.

steps:
  1. Load speedingKmh and stopSec via thresholdsFromVehicleConfig.
  2. In EventsTab, replace the static value span with a numeric input
     for events that have hasValue. Stop the row click from toggling
     when the input is focused.
  3. Pass the edited numbers into mergeVehicleConfigFromEventChecks.
     Delete the read of EVENTS_CONFIG.value on save.
  4. Clamp speeding to 1–360. Keep the existing stop rule: stop events
     on require minStopTime >= 90_000 ms.
  5. Show the server value, not 130, after getvea.

out:
  - src/screens/object-details/components/EventsTab.tsx
  - src/screens/object-details/lib/vehicle-event-config-ui.ts
  - src/screens/object-details/hooks/useObjectDetailsHistory.ts

done:
  - User can set a speeding threshold other than 130 and a stop duration
    other than 90, within the clamps.
  - Apply sends those numbers as speedingValue and minStopTime.
  - Checkbox-only events stay checkbox-only.
